# The door contracts this repo's CI holds its door to: parachute-core `contracts/suites/door` at an exact commit
# (T-431). One suite runs against every way of running Parachute (a box, this hosted door, a personal Cloudflare
# door); `scripts/door-parity.sh` runs it here against both workers under local workerd and compares the result with
# the box's kept fingerprint in that same commit (`contracts/suites/door/golden/`).
#
# This pin is separate from the engine pin (core-source.env) on purpose. The contracts are black-box: they speak HTTP
# and MCP and import nothing from the engine, and they know which release line a door is on. So this pin can follow
# parachute-core `next` while the engine this door runs stays where core-source.env holds it.
#
# Moving it: bump the SHA in its own change and run `bash scripts/door-parity.sh`. A new difference is either drift
# in this door (fix it here) or a difference meant on both sides (name it in parachute-core
# `contracts/suites/door/deliberate.json`, with why and who decides).
DOOR_SUITE_REPO_URL="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-core.git"
#
# door/0.9 runs two doors from this checkout, each against the 0.9.1 box's fingerprint: `cloud` (Parachute Cloud on the
# 0.9 engine, T-456: what Cloud staging serves) and `personal` (the single-owner profile, deploy/personal). The
# harness reads the engine pin's version and runs a 0.9 cloud checkout as `cloud-0.9.1`. Each door is compared with the
# box alone (scripts/door-parity.sh). The `cloud` door against box-0.8 is next's check.
# T-476 (11-21): back on core next, at b1d2da5. It carries core #142 (a one-address personal door is run and described
# as one address; the 60cefc1 side pin on `door-suite/0.9-t476` is no longer needed) and #135 (write lists deleted
# records), which this door now meets with next's #435. Typed keys (#140/#143/#144) and write-defines-types (#134/#139)
# stay named drift in that commit's deliberate.json until this door has them.
# Then core #145 (write-defines-types is no longer drift: this door lets write define a type, parachute-cloud #438),
# and core #148 (typed-keys is no longer drift: this door holds typed keys and the list, parachute-cloud #439).
# 11-22: both merged on core next (8cd910a, 76ed8e9); the pin is back on core next, at its head after the
# 0.9.0-pre.2 changelog line for them (#152). No side pin is left on door/0.9.
DOOR_SUITE_REF="28a3db487e24400043f8a023262b89cbcc48e3eb"
# The box fingerprint this door is compared with (a file in contracts/suites/door/golden/ at that commit).
DOOR_SUITE_GOLDEN="box-0.9.1"
# The doors the suite starts from this checkout, comma-separated: cloud (next), or cloud,personal (door/0.9).
DOOR_SUITE_DOOR="cloud,personal"
